# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION 1: SPRING SECURITY FRAMEWORK
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-22732: Spring Security authorization bypass for non-servlet functional router patterns
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED
# Upstream Affected: Spring Security Web 6.3.x functional routing matchers
# Technical Justification: Vulnerability exists strictly when routing HTTP requests using Spring WebFlux or
# functional RouterFunction endpoint mappings. ShopSphere is built strictly on standard Spring MVC
# Servlet architecture with DispatcherServlet, @RestController classes, and standard AntPathRequestMatcher
# mappings. Furthermore, method security is enforced via @PreAuthorize annotations directly on service methods.
# Compensating Controls: SecurityFilterChain enforces stateless JWT authentication; method security is enabled.
# Security Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-22732

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION 2: SPRING CORE & FRAMEWORK INTERNALS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2025-41249: Spring Core annotation processing reflection condition
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED
# Upstream Affected: Spring Core reflection metadata cache under untrusted class loading
# Technical Justification: The reflection condition requires untrusted classes to be introduced into the
# class loader at runtime. In ShopSphere, class loading is completely static and restricted to the immutable
# container classpath. Zero dynamic class loading or untrusted reflection is performed.
# Compensating Controls: Immutable container filesystem; non-root user execution prevents runtime class tampering.
# Security Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2025-41249

# CVE-2026-41842: Spring Framework Denial of Service when parsing specific HTTP request headers
# Classification: MITIGATED
# Upstream Affected: Spring Framework Web header parsing
# Technical Justification: Vulnerability involves CPU exhaustion when parsing malformed or excessively long
# multi-value headers directly in Spring Framework. In ShopSphere, Spring Boot never receives raw Internet traffic.
# All inbound requests pass through the Nginx reverse proxy which enforces strict RFC header syntax, limits
# client header buffers to 8k (large_client_header_buffers 4 8k), and enforces proxy_read_timeout 60s.
# Compensating Controls: Nginx reverse proxy header normalization, edge buffering, and request timeouts.
# Security Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41842

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION 3: SPRING WEBMVC ROUTING & RENDERING
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-47884: Spring WebMVC path traversal in resource handlers
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED / MITIGATED
# Upstream Affected: Spring WebMVC ResourceHttpRequestHandler serving static resources
# Technical Justification: Spring Boot is configured purely as a headless JSON REST API (all endpoints under /api/v1/*).
# Static file serving is completely handled by Nginx in the frontend container using `try_files $uri =404`.
# No Spring WebMVC static resource locations (classpath:/static/, /public/) are exposed to client routing.
# Compensating Controls: Nginx web server isolates static assets; Spring Boot ResourceHandlerRegistry is disabled.
# Security Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-47884

# CVE-2026-41845: Spring WebMVC Cross-site scripting in error views
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED
# Upstream Affected: Spring MVC server-side HTML error view templates
# Technical Justification: ShopSphere does not use server-side HTML rendering (no JSP, Thymeleaf, or FreeMarker error views).
# The backend is a pure REST JSON API. All errors are caught by GlobalExceptionHandler which serializes a strongly-typed
# ErrorResponse Java record as application/json. Zero HTML is produced by the backend application.
# Compensating Controls: Content-Type: application/json enforced; X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff header set by Nginx.
# Security Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41845

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION 4: SPRING EXPRESSION LANGUAGE (SpEL) & DATA COMMONS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-41850: Spring Expression Language (SpEL) Denial of Service
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED
# Upstream Affected: SpEL expression evaluation engine
# Technical Justification: Vulnerability requires user-supplied expressions to be evaluated by SpEL ExpressionParser.
# In ShopSphere, SpEL is used solely in static compile-time @PreAuthorize annotations (e.g., @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")).
# Zero user input or dynamic runtime expressions are parsed or evaluated by SpEL anywhere in the codebase.
# Compensating Controls: Codebase audit confirms zero SpEL expression parsing of external parameters.
# Security Owner: Java Application Security Engineer
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41850

# CVE-2026-41716: Spring Data Commons DoS via unbounded pagination parameters
# Classification: MITIGATED
# Upstream Affected: Spring Data Commons pageable parameter resolver
# Technical Justification: Potential resource consumption if clients request unbounded page sizes (e.g., size=1000000).
# ShopSphere controllers enforce PageRequest constraints, default page sizes of 10 or 20, and cap maximum page size.
# Compensating Controls: Bounded Pageable validation in controller layer and DB query timeout bounds.
# Security Owner: Application Backend Lead
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-41716

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION 5: SPRING BOOT ACTUATOR & RUNTIME
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CVE-2026-40973: Spring Boot remote code execution in Actuator Jolokia / H2 console endpoints
# Classification: NOT AFFECTED
# Upstream Affected: Actuator Jolokia JMX integration and H2 Web Console
# Technical Justification: Jolokia is not present on the application classpath. The H2 web console is strictly disabled
# in production (spring.h2.console.enabled=false in application-prod.yml). Actuator exposure is strictly restricted
# to health and info endpoints (management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=health,info).
# Compensating Controls: Production configuration explicitly disables H2 console and limits Actuator exposure.
# Security Owner: DevSecOps Engineering
# Review Date: 2027-01-01
CVE-2026-40973
